zsh + oh-my-zsh:
  pkg install zsh
  sh -c "$(wget -O- https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ohmyzsh/ohmyzsh/master/tools/install.sh)"
  chsh -s zsh          # only symlinks ~/.termux/shell; `chsh -s bash` undoes it
  plugins: vi-mode (VI_MODE_SET_CURSOR=true), git, extract, colored-man-pages,
    history-substring-search, zsh-autosuggestions, transient-prompt,
    zsh-syntax-highlighting (must stay LAST)
  custom clones: zsh-autosuggestions, zsh-syntax-highlighting,
    olets/zsh-transient-prompt -> $ZSH_CUSTOM/plugins/transient-prompt
  compinit/compdef are stubbed out before oh-my-zsh: no Tab completion, saves ~45ms
    and avoids the 1.2s zcompdump rebuild. Delete the stubs to restore Tab.
  startup ~285ms (bash ~50ms): oh-my-zsh ~240, vivid ~36, zoxide ~31, fzf ~48,
    zsh itself 33. zsh-completions is installed but $PREFIX/share/zsh/site-functions
    is not in fpath on Termux.
  bash-only lines do not parse: bind, shopt, source <(fzf --bash). Use fzf --zsh and
    zoxide init --cmd cd zsh. palette.sh is bash-only; Ctrl-Space palette is a zle
    widget in .zshrc (^P stays history-up).
  prompt: native 2-line, dir + git status symbols, no branch:
    PROMPT=$'%B%F{cyan}%~%f%b $(git_prompt_status)\n%B%F{cyan}>%f%b '
  transient prompt: set TRANSIENT_PROMPT_PROMPT / _TRANSIENT_PROMPT after PROMPT;
    RPROMPT is the vi-mode indicator.
  remove: rm -rf ~/.oh-my-zsh ~/.zshrc ~/.zsh_history ~/.zcompdump*
    pkg uninstall zsh

zsh + oh-my-zsh (Termux):
  pkg install zsh
  sh -c "$(wget -O- https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ohmyzsh/ohmyzsh/master/tools/install.sh)"
  chsh -s zsh          # only symlinks ~/.termux/shell, nothing in /etc/passwd
  chsh -s bash         # undo
  - bundled plugin vi-mode + VI_MODE_SET_CURSOR=true (block cursor in normal mode)
  - custom plugins cloned to ~/.oh-my-zsh/custom/plugins:
      zsh-autosuggestions, zsh-syntax-highlighting (must be LAST in plugins=())
  - startup ~285ms on this phone (bash ~50ms). Breakdown: oh-my-zsh source ~240,
    vivid ~36, zoxide ~31, fzf ~48; zsh alone is 33.
  - compinit is disabled on purpose (compinit/compdef stubbed out before oh-my-zsh):
    no Tab completion. Saves ~45ms and avoids the 1.2s zcompdump rebuild spike.
    Delete those two stub lines to get Tab back.
  - bash config does NOT parse in zsh: `bind`, `shopt`, `source <(fzf --bash)` all fail.
    Use `source <(fzf --zsh)` and `eval "$(zoxide init --cmd cd zsh)"`.
  - ~/.config/bash/palette.sh is bash-only; Ctrl-Space palette reimplemented as a zle
    widget in ~/.zshrc (Ctrl-P left as history-up)
  - zsh-completions is installed but $PREFIX/share/zsh/site-functions is NOT in fpath on
    Termux; add `fpath=($PREFIX/share/zsh/site-functions $fpath)` before oh-my-zsh to use it
  - remove cleanly: rm -rf ~/.oh-my-zsh ~/.zshrc ~/.zsh_history ~/.zcompdump*
    pkg uninstall zsh zsh-completions
  - prompt is native (no starship): 2-line,
      PROMPT=$'%B%F{cyan}%~%f%b %F{cyan}$(git_prompt_info)%f\n%B%F{cyan}>%f%b '
    Cost measured in a repo: native ~7ms/prompt, starship ~86ms/prompt on this
    phone, so starship is installed but disabled (init line commented in .zshrc).
  - transient prompt: starship has no native zsh support (issue #888), so
    olets/zsh-transient-prompt is cloned to $ZSH_CUSTOM/plugins/transient-prompt
    and added to plugins=() before zsh-syntax-highlighting. It is theme-agnostic:
    set TRANSIENT_PROMPT_PROMPT / _TRANSIENT_PROMPT after the prompt is defined.
  - RPROMPT is owned by the vi-mode indicator via TRANSIENT_PROMPT_RPROMPT.
  - if starship is re-enabled: .config/starship.toml has [profiles] transient and
    the four TRANSIENT_PROMPT_* vars must be assigned after `starship init`.

